    <title>Problems</title>
    <text><table><thead><tr><th>Problem</th><th>Clinical status</th><th>Verification</th><th>Code</th><th>Provenance</th></tr></thead><tbody>
  <tr ID="problem-1">
    <td>Wheeze, cough and breathlessness this winter, for about three months: symptoms on three or four days a week, waking with cough and a tight chest about twice a month, breathless climbing the hill streets in cold air; worse with cold wind, kitchen and fireplace smoke, and colds; called a weak chest and asthma since childhood but never tested or treated. Asthma to be confirmed with spirometry before and after bronchodilator and FeNO</td><td>resolved</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>R06.2</td><td>S — Synthetic presenting problem anchored to her documented frail, asthmatic childhood. Superseded by the diagnosis at the second visit.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-2">
    <td>Asthma, confirmed, mild persistent: variable airflow obstruction (FEV1/FVC 0.72, below the lower limit of normal, rising to 0.80 after bronchodilator; FEV1 2.24 L, 83 percent predicted, rising 330 mL or 15 percent); type 2 inflammation (FeNO 38 ppb, blood eosinophils 0.38 x10^3/uL, total IgE 165, house dust mite sensitization); tuberculosis infection test negative and chest X-ray clear. Triggers: cold air, kitchen and fireplace smoke, colds</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>J45.30</td><td>S — Synthetic modern confirmation linked to her documented frail, asthmatic childhood and her own later descriptions of asthma.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-4">
    <td>Prone to seasickness on boat trips; meclizine for the sea crossing; resolved on her return</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>T75.3XXA</td><td>S — Synthetic travel-related problem.</td>
  </tr>
  <tr ID="problem-5">
    <td>Pregnancy planning: not sexually active and no contraception wanted now; she may wish to have children one day; folic acid by her choice, and asthma care planned before and during any pregnancy</td><td>active</td><td>confirmed</td>
    <td>Z31.69</td><td>S — Synthetic reproductive health counselling; not a claim about her real life.</td>
  </tr></tbody></table></text>

